-- ============================================================
-- Warrior: Heroic Strike and Cleave -- Cataclysm cost model
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Heroic Strike: Consider raising the cost from 15 to 30 ..."
--
-- Both abilities are still on the 3.3.5a "on next swing" model: pressing them
-- queues a bonus onto the next auto-attack rather than doing anything now.
-- Cataclysm replaced that with a plain instant ability at a flat 30 rage, which
-- is what this file implements.
--
-- Four columns move on all 21 ranks:
--   Attributes 327700 -> 327696.  That clears exactly one bit,
--     SPELL_ATTR0_ON_NEXT_SWING_NO_DAMAGE (0x4, SharedDefines.h:372), which is
--     what Spell::IsNextMeleeSwingSpell tests.  Nothing else in the mask moves.
--   ManaCost -> 300.  Rage is stored in tenths, so 300 is 30 rage.  Every rank,
--     including the low ones that cost 15 (Heroic Strike) or 20 (Cleave).
--   Category -> 1229 and CategoryRecoveryTime -> 3000, giving the two abilities
--     one shared 3 second cooldown.  A per-spell RecoveryTime would not be
--     shared, and Category is how the client groups a cooldown sweep too.
--     1229 has to satisfy two things at once: no spell in Spell.dbc may already
--     use it, or that spell joins the shared cooldown; and it must exist as a
--     record in SpellCategory.dbc, which the client looks up for category
--     flags.  Scanning both: 197 of SpellCategory.dbc's 262 ids are referenced
--     by a spell, and 1229 is one of the unreferenced ones, Flags 0 -- the same
--     flags as Charge's category 1219.  An invented id such as 1220 satisfies
--     only the first condition.
--
-- StartRecoveryCategory and StartRecoveryTime stay 0 -- these deliberately do
-- NOT trigger the global cooldown, which is the point of them.  They are rage
-- dumps fired between GCD-bound abilities, and the shared 3 second category
-- cooldown is the only throttle.
--
-- Worth watching in play: as "on next swing" spells, SPELL_EFFECT_WEAPON_DAMAGE
-- added its flat bonus *to* the auto-attack.  As instants they become their own
-- swing -- full weapon damage plus the bonus -- and the auto-attack still
-- lands.  That is the Cataclysm behaviour and is intended, but it is a real
-- damage increase per use on top of the cost change.
--
-- Improved Heroic Strike drops to 1 / 2 / 5 rage.  SPELL_AURA_ADD_FLAT_MODIFIER
-- with EffectMiscValue 14 (SPELLMOD_COST), amount = EffectBasePoints1 + 1 in
-- tenths of rage, so -11 / -21 / -51 is -10 / -20 / -50 = 1 / 2 / 5.  Its
-- description renders $/10;s1 so the text follows on its own, and
-- EffectSpellClassMaskA1 64 already scopes it to Heroic Strike -- Cleave keeps
-- the full 30.
--
-- Spells:
--   78, 284, 285, 1608, 11564, 11565, 11566, 11567, 25286, 29707, 30324,
--   47449, 47450                                    = Heroic Strike ranks 1-13
--   845, 7369, 11608, 11609, 20569, 25231, 47519, 47520 = Cleave ranks 1-8
--   12282 / 12663 / 12664                           = Improved Heroic Strike
-- ============================================================


